  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Procurement Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The EU contribution to the European Procurement Partnership (EuPP) aims at supporting EU partner countries in enhancing the effectiveness and efficiency of their public procurement, through two main channels. First, by supporting the MAPS initiative (Methodology for Assessing Procurement Systems), the EuPP will foster global improvements in public procurement through the development, update and promotion of a methodology for evaluating public procurement systems. Second, the EuPP will help low- and middle-income countries improve their public procurement systems. This will be achieved through targeted capacity development activities and technical assistance for better designing, operationalizing, and implementing public procurement reforms. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Public procurement is a key pillar in the European Commission&apos;s &#xbf;Collect more, Spend better&#xbf; approach, which is notably supporting partner countries in their public finance management reforms. As public procurement is key to ensure good value for money in public investments, this action will also contribute to the effective implementation and scale-up of the Global Gateway strategy.  &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;EuPP is a project launched in a Team Europe approach, with financial contributions from two EU Member States - FR (AFD) and NL (Minbuza) -, as well as Switzerland (SECO). Contributions from additional partners could also be envisaged. &lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
